/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Johnson.ParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 51`, `matAt x 42` and `(x 60, x 61)` are a weak fit of `Johnson.ParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem johnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Johnson.ParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.polyhedron Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.S N 51 42 60 := by
  rw [Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.len_eq Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.par_ok Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.zs_eq Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.weak_ok Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.poly_eq Pose.JohnsonParabiaugmentedDodecahedron.ok

end Nieuwland.Polyhedra
